[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Sicilian Defense: Alapin Variation"]
[Variation "Alapin Variation, Advance Line"]
[ECO "B22"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "e5-wedge,space-advantage"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. e4 c5 2. c3 e6 3. d4 d5
4. e5 { Gains space and shuts in the bishop on c8 behind its own pawns. The chain from c3 to e5 is a firm base. }
4... Nc6
5. Nf3 { Develops and defends the pawn on e5 at once. }
5... Qb6
(5... Nge7 6. Na3)
(5... cxd4 6. cxd4)
6. a3 { Stops ...Bb4 and keeps b4 available as a pawn break if Black plays ...c4. }
6... c4
7. Nbd2 { Develops the knight and attacks the pawn on c4, which Black now has to look after. }
7... Na5
8. Be2 { Develops and prepares to castle. The pawn on c4 can be attacked later with b3. } *
